  "notes": [
    "Landscape card, foliation 8, headed Thm 2. It asserts existence of a universal principal covering for every discrete π and uniqueness of the classifying space in the homotopy category. These assertions are transcribed, not independently proved here. It then forms the associated quotient from a π-space X and writes the beginning/end of a homotopy sequence.",
    "The associated-bundle sequence gives degree 1 for the third term and π0(X) at the end. The inspected third subscript supports 1, so the shared witness reading is retained. The last argument remains V|X: the V-like ink is not silently replaced by the mathematically expected X. The assertion π0(X)=1 requires connected X, which is not explicitly stated on this card. The cancelled Eπ in the right quotient is readable; the small cancelled equality label is not fully recoverable. No date."
  ],
